   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Dear Budgen: Not a single copy of my <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">presentation copies</seg> has yet reached Paris though I have written three times and telegraphed twice! This explains why you have not yet got yours. The moment they arrive I shall send off one to you. The continual strain of this needless worry after all my work is done has made me very nervous. I hope to get my copies by Thursday or Friday.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>sincerely yours</salute> <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                    </closer> </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">The copies of the first edition of <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysses</name> intended for distribution to friends and family. On 28 February Budgen was sent no. 510 of the less expensive copies of <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysses</name> (Sylvia Beach’s <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysses</name> notebook, Harry Ransom Center, University of Texas at Austin).</note>
            </div>
      </body>
